<div class="wrap">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span>Shipping policy</span>
  </nav>
</div>

<section class="wrap wrap-mid" style="padding-bottom:clamp(60px,8vw,110px)">
  <span class="eyebrow">Policy</span>
  <h1 style="margin:14px 0 18px">Shipping policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Where we ship from, what it costs, and what happens if a parcel goes astray.</p>

  <div class="stack-32" style="margin-top:44px">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">Where it ships from</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>Every order is packed by hand and dispatched from our warehouse in <strong class="gold">China</strong>.
          There is no overseas warehouse in the chain and nothing ships from a second location.</p>
        <p>We dispatch within <strong class="gold">48 hours</strong> of your order. That is the whole of the promise:
          no cut-off time to catch, no business-day arithmetic, and the same forty-eight hours whatever time of day
          you ordered and wherever you are reading this from. Your tracking number is emailed to you when the label
          is created, before the carrier has scanned it.</p>
        <p>If something you ordered is not in stock we will tell you within those 48 hours and give you the choice of
          waiting, splitting the shipment, or cancelling that line.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">Delivery time</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>We do not publish a delivery estimate, and that is deliberate rather than an omission. Once a parcel
          leaves us it is carried by an international carrier and cleared by customs in your country. Neither is
          under our control, and a delivery date quoted by a shop is a date the shop cannot guarantee —
          so we do not quote one.</p>
        <p>What we give you instead is the tracking number, from the moment the label exists. It shows every scan
          between our warehouse and your door, so you can see exactly where the parcel is rather than relying on our
          guess about when it will arrive.</p>
        <p>Customs is the one part of the journey that can add time without warning. A parcel held for inspection is
          not lost, and the tracking will normally say so.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">Options and cost</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p><strong class="gold">Standard</strong> — <%= money(store.flatShippingFee) %> flat, and complimentary on
          orders over <%= money(store.freeShippingThreshold) %>. There is no minimum order.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">Express</strong> — <%= money(store.flatShippingFee * 2) %>. Express buys a priority
          service from the carrier, which moves the parcel up the queue once it is handed over. It does not change
          the 48 hours, which is the same either way, and it cannot move a parcel through customs faster.</p>
        <p>Shipping is calculated at checkout and shown before you pay. Nothing is added after you press pay.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">Customs, duties and taxes</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>Duties, import taxes and customs handling charges are the recipient's responsibility and are not collected
          by us — the carrier will ask you for them before delivery. A parcel refused for that reason comes back to
          us and is refunded less the outbound shipping.</p>
        <p>Tea is a food product, and a few countries restrict the import of unprocessed leaf or of foodstuffs
          generally. If we know a destination will not accept a parcel we will say so before you pay rather than
          after. If a parcel is nonetheless seized or destroyed by customs, we refund the product cost in full.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">Packaging</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>Tea travels in a sealed foil pouch inside a tin or a box, and the outer parcel is plain with no indication
          of its contents. Jade and jewellery travel in a padded case inside a rigid box, with any certificate in the
          same parcel. We use paper tape and paper padding, no plastic void fill, and every part of the outer
          packaging is recyclable.</p>
        <p>A gift order can be sent straight to the recipient with the price removed. Say so in the order notes and we
          will leave the invoice out of the parcel and email it to you instead.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">If a parcel is late, lost or damaged</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>If tracking has not moved for <strong class="gold">10 business days</strong>, or shows delivered when
          nothing arrived, tell us at
          <a class="link-underline" href="mailto:<%= company.email %>"><%= company.email %></a>. We open a claim with
          the carrier and either reship or refund — your choice — and we do not make you wait for the carrier's
          answer before we act.</p>
        <p>If a parcel arrives damaged, photograph the box and the contents before you unpack it fully and email us
          the same day. That is what the carrier's claim needs, and it is the difference between a claim that is paid
          and one that is refused. We will replace the item or refund it either way.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">Returns</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>Returns, exchanges and refunds are covered in full by the
          <a class="link-underline" href="/refund">refund &amp; returns policy</a> — the thirty-day window, what can
          and cannot come back, who pays the return postage, and how long the money takes. The short version: thirty
          days, no restocking fee, and we pay the postage when the fault is ours.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">Payment</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>We accept Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Discover, JCB, Diners Club and China UnionPay — credit and
          debit cards, in the currency shown at checkout. Every payment is processed by our payment provider, a
          PCI-DSS compliant payment institution, as a 3-D Secure 2 authenticated card-not-present transaction.</p>
        <p>3-D Secure 2 means your bank may ask you to confirm the payment — usually a code in your banking app, a
          text message, or a fingerprint. This is a security feature of the card scheme, not something we control,
          and it protects you against fraudulent use of your card.</p>
        <p><strong class="gold">We never see or store your card number.</strong> The card details you type go
          straight from your browser to the payment provider over TLS, and are never held on our servers. Our
          database records only the card brand, the last four digits and the provider's transaction identifier, so
          that we can reconcile an order or issue a refund.</p>
        <p>All prices are in <%= store.currency %> and include <%= store.taxLabel %> where applicable, calculated at
          checkout before you pay. We do not store your card for future purchases and there is no one-click
          re-order.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px">3-D Secure and fraud</h3>
      <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.94rem">
        <p>Every card payment on this site is screened in real time for fraud risk before authorisation. If a
          transaction is flagged we may contact you to confirm the order before shipping. A declined payment means
          your card was not charged — an authorisation that is later reversed will show a pending amount on your
          statement which your bank releases on its own schedule.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row" style="gap:12px;margin-top:40px;flex-wrap:wrap">
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/refund">Refund policy</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/terms">Terms of service</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>
    <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/order">Track an order</a>
  </div>
</section>
